1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:02,236
These ruins are
older than humans.

2
00:00:02,256 --> 00:00:03,940
Someone keeps
repairing them.

3
00:00:03,960 --> 00:00:04,940
Meet the Builders.

4
00:00:04,960 --> 00:00:06,507
Their wall still
stands.

5
00:00:06,527 --> 00:00:08,178
The lazy version:
ancient,

6
00:00:08,198 --> 00:00:09,492
mysterious,
gone.

7
00:00:09,512 --> 00:00:10,534
Press run.

8
00:00:10,554 --> 00:00:12,096
A thousand years of
digging.

9
00:00:12,116 --> 00:00:13,670
Nothing but stones.

10
00:00:13,690 --> 00:00:15,336
A ruin that says
nothing is just

11
00:00:15,356 --> 00:00:16,261
rocks.

12
00:00:16,281 --> 00:00:17,256
Good ruins talk.

13
00:00:17,276 --> 00:00:18,219
Four rules.

14
00:00:18,239 --> 00:00:19,752
The fifth is the
twist.

15
00:00:19,772 --> 00:00:21,089
One:
their tools.

16
00:00:21,109 --> 00:00:22,996
A gear that nobody
here can make.

17
00:00:23,016 --> 00:00:24,396
Two:
what they valued.

18
00:00:24,416 --> 00:00:26,150
Their biggest room
was a kitchen.

19
00:00:26,170 --> 00:00:27,468
Three:
how they failed.

20
00:00:27,488 --> 00:00:29,160
Every well is full
of sand.

21
00:00:29,180 --> 00:00:30,497
Four:
their days.

22
00:00:30,517 --> 00:00:32,160
A child's handprints,
pressed into the

23
00:00:32,180 --> 00:00:32,951
mortar.

24
00:00:32,971 --> 00:00:33,788
Run it again.

25
00:00:33,808 --> 00:00:35,038
A thousand years.

26
00:00:35,058 --> 00:00:37,424
Every find opens two
questions.

27
00:00:37,444 --> 00:00:38,199
Rule five?

28
00:00:38,219 --> 00:00:39,186
Look closer.

29
00:00:39,206 --> 00:00:41,157
Half this wall is
newer than us.

30
00:00:41,177 --> 00:00:43,620
Someone replaces one
stone every night.

31
00:00:43,640 --> 00:00:45,104
Nobody has seen them.

32
00:00:45,124 --> 00:00:46,777
So never tell us who.

33
00:00:46,797 --> 00:00:48,315
Show how they lived
and fell.

34
00:00:48,335 --> 00:00:50,437
Every ruin keeps one
secret.

35
00:00:50,457 --> 00:00:51,976
What should
archaeologists never

36
00:00:51,996 --> 00:00:53,214
find in your world?

37
00:00:53,234 --> 00:00:55,032
Part 35 of 50.

38
00:00:55,052 --> 00:00:57,682
Follow for part 36:
two armies are never

39
00:00:57,702 --> 00:00:58,719
enough.
